{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TwistedQuantumDimension","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TwistedQuantumDimension","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.Ribbon","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedQuantumDimension","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RigidTensorDual","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedSlide"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith_tensor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith_tensor","kind":"theorem","line":362,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L362-L372","doc":"**Multiplicativity of the twisted quantum dimension**, unconditionally.\n\n`qDimTwistedWith_tensor_of_monodromy` with its hypothesis discharged by\n`qTrWith_tensor_monodromy`.  This is the ribbon-category fact that the quantum dimension is a\nmonoid homomorphism, for the nested `tensorExactPairing` dual and with no rigidity assumed beyond\nthe two exact pairings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith_tensor_of_monodromy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith_tensor_of_monodromy","kind":"theorem","line":335,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L335-L360","doc":"**Multiplicativity, CONDITIONAL on the monodromy factorisation.**\n\nThe hypothesis `hmono` is `qTrWith_tensor_monodromy` above, proved unconditionally as of bean\n`qou-l64i`; the unconditional form is `qDimTwistedWith_tensor` below.  This conditional form is kept\nbecause it isolates where the balancing axiom is used.  Closing the 2-cable `X ⊗ Y` with a\nmonodromy `β_{X,Y} ≫ β_{Y,X}` on the input splits into the two separate closures.  Given it, the\ntwisted quantum dimension is multiplicative, and the derivation uses the balancing axiom exactly\nonce — `twist_tensor` is precisely what puts the required monodromy in front of `θ_X ⊗ θ_Y`.\n\nIt was stated conditionally on purpose.  I had asserted in the bean that multiplicativity \"is then\na corollary\"; that assertion is what this theorem replaces with a machine-checked implication, after\nan earlier assertion of the same kind (that the nested closure factors through `ptrWith`) turned out\nto be false.  A named hypothesis discharged by `rw` is worth more than a claim that a step will go\nthrough. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qTrWith_tensor_monodromy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qTrWith_tensor_monodromy","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L252-L333","doc":"**The monodromy factorisation for the nested closure** (bean `qou-l64i`).\n\nClosing the 2-cable `X ⊗ Y` against the nested dual `Y' ⊗ X'` of `tensorExactPairing`, with a\nmonodromy `β_{X,Y} ≫ β_{Y,X}` inserted in front of `g ⊗ h`, splits into the two separate closures.\n\nThe monodromy is not decoration: `tensorExactPairing` nests the two dual pairs in **opposite orders\nat its two ends** — the cup is `X, Y, Y', X'` (X outside) while the cap is `Y', X', X, Y` (Y\noutside) — so the nested closure links the `X`-loop with the `Y`-loop.  The monodromy is exactly the\ncrossing that unlinks them, which is why the statement is false without it.  This is also why the\nearlier attempt to route the proof through a partial trace (`ptrWith`) could not work: no\ntrace-of-partial-trace factorisation respects two opposite nestings at once.\n\nProof shape: the hexagon splits `β_{X⊗Y, Y'⊗X'}` into the `X`- and `Y`-halves; braiding naturality\ndetaches the `X`-strand onto the cup and then carries `g` and `h` back to the two loops; what is\nleft is a single strand crossing a cap, discharged by `braiding_slide_cap_right`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ptrWith_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ptrWith_id","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L237-L249","doc":"**The partial trace of the identity is the dimension**, acting on `X` through the right unitor.\n\n`End(𝟙_C)` acts on every hom-set by whiskering-and-unitors, and this says the partial trace of\n`𝟙_{X⊗Y}` over `Y` is exactly `qDimWith Y Y'` acting on `X` that way — the categorical form of\n\"tracing out a factor multiplies by its dimension\".\n\nThis is the FIRST of the two steps the multiplicativity route needs (bean `qou-l64i`, route 1). The\nsecond — that the *nested* closure of `X ⊗ Y` factors as a full trace of a partial trace — is the\ncrux and is NOT proved here; its statement is recorded in that bean. Do not read this lemma as\nprogress on the nesting: it deliberately sits on the easy side of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ptrWith","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ptrWith","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L232-L235","doc":"**Right partial trace over `Y`**, relative to a chosen pairing `Y ⊣ Y'`: close only the `Y`\nstrand of an endomorphism of `X ⊗ Y`, leaving an endomorphism of `X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qTrWith_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qTrWith_twist","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L229-L230","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qTrWith_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qTrWith_id","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L226-L227","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qTrWith","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qTrWith","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L217-L224","doc":"**Braided trace of an ENDOMORPHISM**, relative to a chosen pairing: `η ≫ (f ▷ B) ≫ β ≫ ε`.\n\nThis is the common generalisation of the two dimensions in this file — `qDimWith` is its value at\n`𝟙`, `qDimTwistedWith` its value at `θ`, recorded as `qTrWith_id` and `qTrWith_twist` below. Having\nit is what lets a *partial* trace be composed with a full one, which is the shape the\nmultiplicativity route needs (bean `qou-l64i`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith_unit","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L203-L211","doc":"**At the monoidal unit the twist is invisible**: `θ_𝟙 = 𝟙` is a `BalancedCategory` axiom, so\nthe twisted and twistless dimensions of the unit agree unconditionally.\n\nThis is why nothing in the RT-input vacuum normalisation moves when the twistless trace is\ncorrectly renamed: `qDim_unit` is a statement about `𝟙_C`, and at `𝟙_C` there is no difference to\nbe made. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith_eq_qDimWith_of_twist_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith_eq_qDimWith_of_twist_id","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L192-L201","doc":"**The twistless dimension is exactly the `θ = 𝟙` case.**  The module docstring asserts this;\nhere it is as a lemma, so the claim is backed rather than merely stated.\n\nNote the hypothesis is *pointwise* — only `θ_A = 𝟙` is required, not `θ = 𝟙` globally.  So this\nalso covers an object that happens to be transparent in an otherwise non-trivially balanced\ncategory, which is the case one actually meets. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedLeftWith_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedLeftWith_eq","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L171-L186","doc":"**Ribbon ⇒ spherical**: in a ribbon category the left and right twisted quantum dimensions of\nevery object agree.\n\nThis is the statement that is *unavailable* for the twistless trace `qDimWith`, and the reason is\nvisible in the proof: the cap identity is discharged by `RibbonCategory.twist_dual` together with\n`rightAdjointMate_comp_evaluation` at `f = θ_X`, and with `θ = 𝟙` both sides of the cap identity\ncollapse to `ε` — true, but then `qDimTwistedLeftWith` and `qDimTwistedWith` are two *different*\ntwistless closures (`(β_ B A).inv` versus `(β_ A B).hom`) whose difference is the monodromy, and no\naxiom of a braided rigid category forces that to vanish.  So the twistless pair is not made\nspherical by this argument at any twist, including the trivial one; it is the twist that carries the\nstatement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedLeftWith_eq_of_cap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedLeftWith_eq_of_cap","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L139-L169","doc":"**Sphericality, reduced to one identity at the cap.**\n\nLeft trace = right trace *as soon as* the two twists agree across the evaluation,\n\n    (θ_B ▷ A) ≫ ε  =  (B ◁ θ_A) ≫ ε.\n\nEverything else is the balancing axiom.  Read as a decomposition this says exactly where the\ncontent of sphericality sits: the Joyal–Street axiom `θ_{A⊗B} = β_{A,B} ≫ β_{B,A} ≫ (θ_A ⊗ θ_B)`\ndoes all of the geometric work — it converts the *left* closure into the *right* one by feeding the\ndouble braiding through the coevaluation — and leaves behind precisely one residue, the twist that\nended up on the dual leg.  A braided category alone cannot discharge that residue, because nothing\nrelates `θ_B` to `θ_A`.  That is the job of the ribbon axiom, and it is the whole job. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedLeftWith","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedLeftWith","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L108-L137","doc":"**The twisted LEFT quantum dimension**: the same strand closed on the other side, carrying the\n*inverse* twist.\n\n**The inverse is load-bearing, so it needs a justification that is not \"it makes the theorem\ncome out\".**  `qDimTwistedLeftWith_eq_of_cap` works precisely because `θ_A` meets `θ_A⁻¹` and\ncancels; with `θ_A` on both sides one is left with `θ_A²`, and the identity would require\n`θ² = 𝟙`, which is false in general.  So the exponent is not cosmetic and cannot be waved through.\n\nTwo things justify it, and it is worth separating them:\n\n1. **The opposite-exponent shape is the standard one.**  Barrett–Westbury, *Spherical Categories*,\n   Prop. 3.6, give the two traces of a spherical Hopf algebra as `tr_L(θ) = tr(θw)` and\n   `tr_R(θ) = tr(θw⁻¹)` — the same element in the two traces, with opposite exponents.\n2. **That shape does not smuggle in sphericality.**  This is the non-circularity check, and it is\n   the more important of the two: Barrett–Westbury's Example 3.5 — the quantised enveloping algebra\n   of the Borel of `SL₂(ℂ)` — uses *this very convention* to exhibit a category satisfying every\n   spherical axiom **except** that \"the left and right traces are distinct\".  A convention under\n   which sphericality is still refutable is not one that assumes it.\n\n**What this does NOT establish, stated so it is not read as more than it is.**  Barrett–Westbury's\n`w` is the **pivotal element** (`γ²(b) = w b w⁻¹`), *not* the ribbon twist `θ`.  The two are related\nin a ribbon category but are not the same object.  So the citation supports the *shape* of this\ndefinition and its non-circularity; it is **not** a citation that this particular `θ`/`θ⁻¹` pairing\nis the standard ribbon left trace.  Establishing that identification would need Turaev's\nconstruction of the left duality from the right one, which is not formalised here.\n\n-- Ref: [barrett1993] Barrett, Westbury, *Spherical Categories*, Prop. 3.6 and Example 3.5. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith_rightDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith_rightDual","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L77-L104","doc":"**Conjugation symmetry of the twisted quantum dimension**, `dim(Xᘁ) = dim(X)`.\n\nThis is where the ribbon axiom earns its place, and it is used exactly once:\n`RibbonCategory.twist_dual` rewrites `θ_{Xᘁ}` to `(θ_X)ᘁ`, and `rightAdjointMate_comp_evaluation`\nat `f = θ_X` carries that mate across the evaluation.  Everything else is braiding naturality and\n`qDimTwistedWith_congr_dual`, which moves to the swapped pairing exhibiting `X` as a right dual\nof `Xᘁ`.\n\nContrast `qDimWith_rightDual`, which needs no axiom at all — that is the price of the twist, and\nit is the whole price. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith_congr_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith_congr_dual","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L60-L75","doc":"**The twisted quantum dimension does not depend on the choice of right dual** — and, unlike\nconjugation symmetry below, this needs **no ribbon axiom**.\n\nThe twist acts on `A`; the comparison `rightDualIso` acts on the dual leg.  They are disjoint, so\nthe twistless proof goes through with one interchange step added. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith_twist_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith_twist_right","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L54-L58","doc":"The twist may be taken on either side of the braiding — braiding naturality, nothing more. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TwistedQuantumDimension.lean#L48-L52","doc":"**The twisted (classical ribbon) quantum dimension**, relative to a chosen exact pairing:\n`η ≫ (θ_A ▷ B) ≫ β ≫ ε`.  Setting `θ = 𝟙` recovers `qDimWith`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}